because I had bounded the parameter at 0 and so it didn't seem it should
generate 0 as a candidate value.  Since 0 <= 0 that expectation is
probably unreasonable, although I thought, as a matter of implementation
if not principle, that variables would never take on the value at the
bounds.

>
