be in order for it?

I think the model below may be mixing two things, because
you have a scalar kappa but use it as kappa[n].

Boost fixed an issue in 1.55 that they describe as:

* Fix issue in Bessel I and K function continued fractions that causes spurious over/underflow.

see:  http://www.boost.org/users/history/version_1_55_0.html

I don't see anything that would let it work on the log scale.

