>>         alpha <- exp(alpha_log);
>>         beta <- exp(beta_log);
>>         gamma <- exp(gamma_log);
>>
>>     Have you plotted your data to see what the relationship between
>> rice[i,j]
>>     and water[i,j] looks like, with and without log transforms?
>>
>>     What's the motivation for using this discontinuous model rather
>> than some
>>     more standard positive-constrained GLM for rice[i,j]?  I'd be
>> tempted to
>>     start with something much simpler, like
>>
>>        log(rice[i,j]) ~ normal(xi[i] * water[i,j] + delta[i], sigma);
>>
>>     and draw (delta[i], xi[i]) from a bivariate normal hierarchical
>> prior.
>>
>>     This changes the functional relationships quite a bit, which is
>> why I renamed
>>     the variables to delta and xi, which are now unconstrained. The
>> reason not to
>>     the parameterization beta[i] * (water[i,j] - gamma[i]), even in
