>     resulting from stan(fit = ..., data = ..., ...) in R, and how this information can be pulled.

It's in the doc for stanfit-class.  You want get_adaptation_info.

But we definitely need better, more tutorial doc.  It's on my
short-term to-do list.  We keep thinking we're going to write a book
about it, but getting some better doc out would be nice.

The problem is that it's grown organically, and the doc is in the usual
R-doc format with everything documented where it lives in the code, not
necessarily where it lives conceptually for users.

> Thanks for thinking with me!

We really want to help people fit hard models.

- Bob

