On Tue, Feb 18, 2014 at 8:47 PM, Luc Coffeng <lucco...@gmail.com> wrote:
> Interestingly, rstan v2.2.0 does seem to manage when I give it the stan-fit S4 object from v1.3.0 to work with (rather than compiling the model in v2.2.0).

Here I am afraid that you are using the compiled model from 1.3 in 2.2.  So in fact, v1.3 is used.  The stanfit object includes the binary shared object (dynamic link library) created from compiling the c++ code for the model.  When a saved stanfit object is reused, the shared object would be loaded and get executed for sampling.  So in v2.2, it would recompile the c++ code when using a stanfit object created in 1.3.  (I am not sure it's a bug or not, but this scenario is rare.)

Jiqiang

