The problem is evident in the metric elements, which fall to very small values in 2.2.0.  This
happens when your chain gets stuck during adaptation such that the covariance becomes
very small.  In 1.3.0 the covariance was normalized so that the global scale canceled out, but
that really masked the issue (not the large number of iterations that failed after a single leapfrog
step — this is indicative of some region of parameter space behaving very poorly).

My best guess is that your model has funky tails that are causing problems, but it would take
some serious investigation to narrow down the exact source of the problem.  That said, the
fact that the log of CDFs can very quickly hit infinity is something of which to be aware.

