Thanks Michael!

Took me a while to understand what you said, but it makes sense to me now. I assume that iterations that fail after a single leapfrog step are reflected by treedepth = 0, or is it -1?

The funky tail business can be explained by the cyclical pattern in the regression line. You could theoretically shift the regression line by one period and scale it by the reproduction factor so that it still fits the data. I tried to anchor the model to prevent this (by making sure that the log CDF would be close to -Inf for unlikely values), but apparently this now backfires with the mass matrix no longer being normalized. I guess another way to do it would be to truncate some of the distributions; there is reasonable prior knowledge of what the parameter values should(n't) be and maybe I just wasn't telling it very well to the model :).

Luc

